lenses.brief:
What the player sees, judged from the first-person sheets in captures_dir (street/, roofs/, boss/, and the arc-* crowd acts). Check that:
- barriers, doorways and drops read as what they are;
- the GO cue points the right way and reads;
- a spawn behind the player arrives unseen;
- the pipe can be found;
- the boss arena reads as closed;
- the seams between sections are clean from both sides (z -53 and z -83);
- the arcs show: a front line of Punks, with waiters standing back from the fray.
Cite each finding with its sheet, tile and time.

Code, tests and pipeline, over the diff from main (git diff main...HEAD):
- the §2 contracts as landed, against ARCHITECTURE.md's '## Level blockout (Milestone 5)';
- no numbers in scripts (tunables in tuning_data.gd's groups);
- the layer rules (the GO cue, F3 and the HUD only read state);
- readability thresholds moved only with a log entry and a twin;
- the done-when test is honest (no forced clears, no assertion that can't fail);
- named spawns can't stall a wave;
- the suite's growth in tests and time, against M4's 1588 tests and 267 s.
